{"id": "EUVD-2026-108847", "enisaUuid": "a2f80647-f56e-31a9-8876-d9791fe88e4c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: preserve NATIVE_LABELS on already-initialized sb in set_mnt_opts\n\nWhen an NFSv4 filesystem exported with security_label is mounted a\nsecond time, sget_fc() returns the existing superblock and\nnfs_get_root() calls security_sb_set_mnt_opts() again on it. Since the\nsuperblock is already SB_INITIALIZED, selinux_set_mnt_opts() takes an\nearly exit without setting SECURITY_LSM_NATIVE_LABELS in\n*set_kern_flags. nfs_get_root() then sees kflags without\nSECURITY_LSM_NATIVE_LABELS set and clears NFS_CAP_SECURITY_LABEL on\nthe shared nfs_server, silently disabling per-file labeling for both\nthe new and the original mount.\n\nCommit 3815a245b501 (\"security/selinux: fix SECURITY_LSM_NATIVE_LABELS\non reused superblock\") fixed the same problem in\nselinux_sb_clone_mnt_opts().  The reused-superblock path for a plain\nsecond mount now goes through sb_set_mnt_opts rather than\nsb_clone_mnt_opts, so it needs the same treatment: on both\nSE_SBINITIALIZED early exits, set SECURITY_LSM_NATIVE_LABELS in\n*set_kern_flags when the superblock was already using\nSECURITY_FS_USE_NATVE.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a545def625860d4ccedc14fe45e884a62a041cef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6da93c625b3557dd23ff6db45d2d1bafeae1565", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5509d498e1b9edafebd5a60ba3cb9ecfda23dc2b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c997832414f1d846de0a1fa38d7d4f62ba2ea917", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28b7260548af3d35773477993ad4e4de41578dd7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99052"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03e570e8-106b-3f9e-a573-fa48baa65e49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1349b677-8921-3c78-a82e-9fbe137777c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "38d95886-aaf0-3f71-817c-a217280bdd1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "46e9956e-68d7-3239-9edf-af5aec952b61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb9ae686507bc5a5ca78e6b3fbe629cd5cc67864 <5509d498e1b9edafebd5a60ba3cb9ecfda23dc2b"}, {"id": "4814e2fd-f3a3-397f-bbe1-35ecb36fea54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "4832e7a5-b3a7-3721-b9ea-54d21c91f519", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "89b93c7f-a2c2-33f3-adb4-e3b2918ff864", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "94747f8e-ba06-3ba2-a7fe-d351fdfaad88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb9ae686507bc5a5ca78e6b3fbe629cd5cc67864 <a545def625860d4ccedc14fe45e884a62a041cef"}, {"id": "b5c80da2-a91e-349c-8d3b-951c64a9004f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb9ae686507bc5a5ca78e6b3fbe629cd5cc67864 <c997832414f1d846de0a1fa38d7d4f62ba2ea917"}, {"id": "c9ee65ad-fdcc-3176-80e8-a3a23ef1c53a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb9ae686507bc5a5ca78e6b3fbe629cd5cc67864 <28b7260548af3d35773477993ad4e4de41578dd7"}, {"id": "f5211809-e939-335d-85a1-070e35c7a5bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb9ae686507bc5a5ca78e6b3fbe629cd5cc67864 <a6da93c625b3557dd23ff6db45d2d1bafeae1565"}, {"id": "f93f792c-92cc-3e30-8a3d-7d093a9d0d54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a751b79a-20f3-3ad7-a74c-d38b47a45121", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": f